# The repository stores LF; the working tree does too, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git's `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) checks the
# files out as CRLF, and `pnpm prettier:check` then reports every file in the
# repo as unformatted — because prettier is configured with `endOfLine: 'lf'`
# and the working tree disagrees with it. The 134 "failures" were a line-ending
# artefact of the machine, not of the code, and they made a real check
# unreadable.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` says: normalise to LF in the repository, and check out
# with LF too. Nothing changes in the history — the blobs were already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touched.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
